    termsParagraph2: "<p class=\"muted\">Using this site's practice questions does not fulfill any part of Minnesota's notary public application process — including the application submitted to the Secretary of State, the $120 nonrefundable application fee, and the oath of office (Minn. Stat. § 359.01) — and does not issue any official notary commission. Minnesota does not require a pre-commissioning training course or a state-administered exam for the base notary commission; notaries are appointed and commissioned directly by the Governor, with the advice and consent of the Senate, and — unlike most states — Minnesota requires no surety bond and no errors-and-omissions insurance for the base commission. Notaries who wish to perform remote online notarizations must separately register that capability with the Secretary of State and certify their technology under Minn. Stat. § 358.645 (the Remote Online Notarization Act), a distinct step with no exam of its own. Completing practice questions here does not fulfill that registration, and does not register you for, or schedule, any part of the official commissioning or Remote Online Notarization process. While we strive to align our content with the current Minnesota Statutes Chapters 358 and 359, it is provided \"as-is\" for self-study and does not constitute legal advice or a guaranteed outcome.</p>",
    examIntroDisclaimer: "register you for, or count toward, the real Minnesota notary commissioning process administered by the Governor and Secretary of State, or the separate section 358.645 Remote Online Notarization registration.",
