    termsParagraph2: "<p class=\"muted\">Using this site's practice questions does not fulfill any part of Mississippi's notary application process — including the oath of office prescribed by Section 268 of the Mississippi Constitution and the $5,000 surety bond (or its functional equivalent) required by Mississippi Code § 25-34-41(3)-(4) — and does not issue any official notary commission or course-completion certificate, because Mississippi requires neither a pre-commission training course nor a graded exam for a standard commission. Applicants qualify by meeting § 25-34-41(2)'s eligibility criteria (at least 18 years old; a U.S. citizen or permanent legal resident; a Mississippi resident for the 30 days immediately preceding application; able to read and write English; and not disqualified under § 25-34-43), executing the oath of office, filing the $5,000 surety bond, and paying the Secretary of State's application fee — after which the Secretary of State issues a four-year commission under § 25-34-41(5). Completing practice questions here also does not register you for, or submit, that official application. While we strive to align our content with the current Mississippi Code Title 25, Chapter 34 — \"The Revised Mississippi Law on Notarial Acts\" — it is provided \"as-is\" for self-study and does not constitute legal advice or a guaranteed outcome.</p>",
